{"nodes": [{"id": "docs_core_scheduling_scheduling_refactor", "label": "Scheduling refactor", "file_type": "concept", "source_file": "docs/core/scheduling.md", "source_location": null, "source_url": null, "captured_at": null, "author": null, "contributor": null, "rationale": "Two competing schedulers (core Scheduler + Nexus SystemScheduler) reconciled by hand in GameplayPlugin, plus 4 latent bugs meaning public contracts never ran; Nexus becomes a pure data store with ordering owned by one authority."}, {"id": "docs_core_scheduling_lane", "label": "Lane (fixed | update | render)", "file_type": "concept", "source_file": "docs/core/scheduling.md", "source_location": null, "source_url": null, "captured_at": null, "author": null, "contributor": null}, {"id": "docs_core_scheduling_stage_vocabulary", "label": "Named stage vocabulary (Stages.ts)", "file_type": "concept", "source_file": "docs/core/scheduling.md", "source_location": null, "source_url": null, "captured_at": null, "author": null, "contributor": null, "rationale": "Numeric priorities overflowed their band without guardrails (gizmo 700+id), expressed no relation, and coupled every package to PRIORITY literals; a closed per-lane enum forces coarse ordering changes through reviewed vocabulary instead of magic numbers."}, {"id": "docs_core_scheduling_stepspec", "label": "StepSpec (before / after constraints)", "file_type": "concept", "source_file": "docs/core/scheduling.md", "source_location": null, "source_url": null, "captured_at": null, "author": null, "contributor": null, "rationale": "Fine ordering resolved by Kahn topo sort WITHIN a stage only (cross-stage edges are a clear error), with insertion order as stable tiebreak; pure before/after was rejected as under-constrained with unreadable errors."}, {"id": "docs_core_scheduling_stephandle", "label": "StepHandle", "file_type": "concept", "source_file": "docs/core/scheduling.md", "source_location": null, "source_url": null, "captured_at": null, "author": null, "contributor": null, "rationale": "onUpdate/onFixedUpdate/onRender returned void, so uninstall leaked steps (NebulaPlugin.unsubscribe always null, EditorPlugin could not remove picking/gizmo)."}, {"id": "docs_core_scheduling_stepset", "label": "StepSet (groups)", "file_type": "concept", "source_file": "docs/core/scheduling.md", "source_location": null, "source_url": null, "captured_at": null, "author": null, "contributor": null, "rationale": "Lets editor mode and scenes toggle whole groups at zero cost (steps stay registered, just disabled) and remove them wholesale at teardown."}, {"id": "docs_core_scheduling_stepcontext", "label": "StepContext (dt, alpha, tick, frame, elapsed)", "file_type": "concept", "source_file": "docs/core/scheduling.md", "source_location": null, "source_url": null, "captured_at": null, "author": null, "contributor": null, "rationale": "A bare dt cannot carry alpha/tick, so every step signature had to change; the phase-0 compat fa\u00e7ade deferred the chore and phase 8 assumed it."}, {"id": "docs_core_scheduling_advancefixed", "label": "Engine.advanceFixed seam", "file_type": "concept", "source_file": "docs/core/scheduling.md", "source_location": null, "source_url": null, "captured_at": null, "author": null, "contributor": null, "rationale": "The single seam that keeps rollback netcode possible without building it today: a netcode driver would call advanceFixed with a per-tick input snapshot, outside RAF."}, {"id": "docs_core_scheduling_frameclock", "label": "FrameClock", "file_type": "concept", "source_file": "docs/core/scheduling.md", "source_location": null, "source_url": null, "captured_at": null, "author": null, "contributor": null, "rationale": "Monotonic tick/frame/elapsed/acc via performance.now; Date.now is banned in the fixed lane because the sim must be a pure function of (tick, fixedDelta, input snapshot)."}, {"id": "docs_core_scheduling_topological_plugin_boot", "label": "Topological plugin boot (provides / requires)", "file_type": "concept", "source_file": "docs/core/scheduling.md", "source_location": null, "source_url": null, "captured_at": null, "author": null, "contributor": null, "rationale": "Declares the DI contract already implicit in services.wait/provide; fixes the boot hang (a missing dep used to wait forever) via MissingDependencyError, DependencyCycleError, a boot timeout, and a post-install assertion."}, {"id": "docs_core_scheduling_fixed_step_determinism", "label": "Fixed-step determinism (rollback-ready, not deterministic)", "file_type": "rationale", "source_file": "docs/core/scheduling.md", "source_location": null, "source_url": null, "captured_at": null, "author": null, "contributor": null, "rationale": "Under the RAF driver (dt clamp 0.25 + maxSubSteps dropping time) the sim is NOT bit-exact across machines; the design is rollback-ready (advanceFixed seam + no wall-clock in sim), not deterministic today."}, {"id": "docs_core_scheduling_registersystem", "label": "registerSystem adapter", "file_type": "concept", "source_file": "docs/core/scheduling.md", "source_location": null, "source_url": null, "captured_at": null, "author": null, "contributor": null, "rationale": "Narrows StepContext to {world, dt} so gameplay systems register as ordinary scheduler steps, replacing the deleted SystemScheduler and the monolithic update()."}, {"id": "docs_core_scheduling_scenecontext_scheduler", "label": "SceneContext.scheduler (scene-scoped StepSet)", "file_type": "concept", "source_file": "docs/core/scheduling.md", "source_location": null, "source_url": null, "captured_at": null, "author": null, "contributor": null, "rationale": "Makes scenes first-class schedulable citizens with no special case: SceneManager creates one set per active scene, auto-removed on destroy()."}, {"id": "docs_core_scheduling_engine_loop", "label": "Engine loop: fixed\u00d7N \u2192 update \u2192 render+alpha", "file_type": "concept", "source_file": "docs/core/scheduling.md", "source_location": null, "source_url": null, "captured_at": null, "author": null, "contributor": null, "rationale": "Running fixed before update changes feel (variable logic sees post-sim state in the same frame) but marries the interpolated render; scene.update became a registered step so there is no second inline entry point."}], "edges": [{"source": "docs_core_scheduling_scheduling_refactor", "target": "docs_core_nexus_ecs_nexus_ecs", "relation": "references", "confidence": "EXTRACTED", "confidence_score": 1.0, "source_file": "docs/core/scheduling.md", "source_location": null, "weight": 1.0}, {"source": "docs_core_scheduling_scheduling_refactor", "target": "docs_core_scheduling_lane", "relation": "references", "confidence": "EXTRACTED", "confidence_score": 1.0, "source_file": "docs/core/scheduling.md", "source_location": null, "weight": 1.0}, {"source": "docs_core_scheduling_scheduling_refactor", "target": "docs_core_scheduling_stage_vocabulary", "relation": "references", "confidence": "EXTRACTED", "confidence_score": 1.0, "source_file": "docs/core/scheduling.md", "source_location": null, "weight": 1.0}, {"source": "docs_core_scheduling_scheduling_refactor", "target": "docs_core_scheduling_stepspec", "relation": "references", "confidence": "EXTRACTED", "confidence_score": 1.0, "source_file": "docs/core/scheduling.md", "source_location": null, "weight": 1.0}, {"source": "docs_core_scheduling_scheduling_refactor", "target": "docs_core_scheduling_stephandle", "relation": "references", "confidence": "EXTRACTED", "confidence_score": 1.0, "source_file": "docs/core/scheduling.md", "source_location": null, "weight": 1.0}, {"source": "docs_core_scheduling_scheduling_refactor", "target": "docs_core_scheduling_stepset", "relation": "references", "confidence": "EXTRACTED", "confidence_score": 1.0, "source_file": "docs/core/scheduling.md", "source_location": null, "weight": 1.0}, {"source": "docs_core_scheduling_scheduling_refactor", "target": "docs_core_scheduling_engine_loop", "relation": "references", "confi